 "stimulus_html": "<figure id=\"BRI_APUSH_11_03_Influenza\" class=\"scaled-down-70\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/2864be0dde74d4a8.png\" alt=\"The broadside reads “Treasury Department. United States Public Health Service. Influenza. Spread by droplets sprayed from nose and throat. Cover each cough and sneeze with handkerchief. Spread by contact. Avoid crowds. If possible, walk to work. Do not spit on floor or sidewalk. Do not use common drinking cups and common towels. Avoid excessive fatigue. If taken ill, go to bed and send for a doctor. The above applies also to colds, bronchitis, pneumonia, and tuberculosis.”\">\n\n<figcaption>A 1919 public health broadside provides information on the Spanish flu pandemic.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p><i>Refer to the image provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 616103,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The information presented in the broadside at the provided link could be used to support which of the following conclusions?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1172381,
     "content_html": "The government developed public policies for fighting the disease."
    },
    {
     "id": 1172380,
     "content_html": "Private business banned individuals on the basis of their health status."
    },
    {
     "id": 1172379,
     "content_html": "Censorship impeded the spread of information about the disease."
    },
    {
     "id": 1172378,
     "content_html": "Widespread panic set in because there was little understanding of the way the disease spread."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 616104,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The publication of this broadside most likely indicates",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1172384,
     "content_html": "an expansion of the role of the federal government"
    },
    {
     "id": 1172385,
     "content_html": "the widespread health concerns caused by the epidemic"
    },
    {
     "id": 1172383,
     "content_html": "the national government’s concern about the effects of the epidemic on trade"
    },
    {
     "id": 1172382,
     "content_html": "the ignorance of most citizens of the time about healthy habits"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 616105,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The situation that prompted the broadside can be best described as",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1172388,
     "content_html": "the Red Scare created a fear of socialism in America"
    },
    {
     "id": 1172387,
     "content_html": "people feared America becoming involved in another European war if the United States joined the League of Nations"
    },
    {
     "id": 1172386,
     "content_html": "the rebirth of the Ku Klux Klan led a fear that personal freedoms would be lost"
    },
    {
     "id": 1172389,
     "content_html": "a devastating Spanish flu epidemic spread fear, misery, and death around the world"
    }
   ],
